After a little while, a woman comes to the counter.
She wants a coffee.
Sunita looks at me.
She says, 'Maya, you make this coffee.'
I take a deep breath.
My first coffee was not good.
Then, the milk was too hot.
But I am learning to make good coffee.
This is my second coffee.
Now I work carefully.
I remember Sunita's instructions.
I start the machine.
I heat the milk.
This time, the milk is perfect.
I pour the milk into the cup.
The foam on top of the coffee is also excellent.
This second coffee looks much better.
Sunita smiles.
She says, 'Very good.'
I am happy.
